{
  "queries": [],
  "result_json": "{\"reviews\":[{\"actor\":\"moss\",\"decision\":\"develop\",\"ability\":null,\"reason\":\"The related-capability search and supplied contracts do not establish an equivalent edge-production operation. gather transfers loose stone but does not shape it; probe supports limited observation or small physical tests, not calibrated edge certification; thin-slice-food-drying-trial consumes the required tool condition without producing it. Develop a general material shaping-and-assessment operation, with a useful executable selection/inspection precursor when shaping tools or measurement equipment are absent. Neither the visible source nor development guarantees a qualifying edge.\",\"specification\":\"General operation: Shape and assess a material tool. Parameters: mode select/shape/inspect, exact source or owned inputStackId, quantity, intended contact requirements, optional exact toolIds, supportId and instrumentIds. Applicable to any actor and suitable material, not this stone instance alone. Initial executable modes select and inspect inspect accessible surfaces and record actual visible condition; shape enables only mechanically supported methods with real equipment. Record reuse of forest.gather, forest.pickup, base:navigate and open.probe observation semantics; do not relabel their code as new invention. Existing thin-slice-food-drying-trial remains unchanged. Dependencies entering this conversation's implementation handoff: persistent material/fragment identity and mass accounting, bounded shaping/contact mechanics, tool wear and evidence-qualified inspection. If these mechanisms are missing, implement the selection/inspection precursor rather than inventing a successful shaping result. No world time passes during development or review. Exact initial reference is start-2-stone at (11,20.5), observed stock 7, suitability unknown; it is not owned equipment. Travel uses navigate: speed 0.8 and actual distance times 2 energy increased by carried mass, with actual obstacles. Actor position and path are not supplied, so no exact travel total is asserted. At source reach, select costs one round and 0.2 energy and identifies only accessible loose candidates and visible defects. Gathering one genuinely accessible loose unit uses gather, one round, 2 energy and decrements actual source stock by one; no quarrying or guaranteed flint. Ground pickup, if needed instead, uses pickup at one round and 1 + 0.2 times transferred mass energy. Gathering does not both consume stock and create an additional duplicate ground unit. Initial assessment needs daylight or another actual adequate light source and a reachable stable work location; direct visual inspection costs one round and 0.2 energy. No other tools are assumed. A naturally edged candidate can be retained without shaping, but visual inspection alone cannot establish the requested radius, hardness, absence of all fractures or contamination. Report each property as observed, measured with its evidence and uncertainty, failed, or unverified. The target contract is radius <=0.0002 in the contact model's length units, hardness >=8 in its hardness scale, not fractured and not contaminated. Verify scale/units rather than substituting a guessed scale. A qualifying assessment requires actual suitably resolving edge metrology, appropriate hardness test equipment/reference and a valid fracture/contamination examination method; no such equipment or reference is established here. Optional instrumentIds must resolve to acquired, applicable equipment with calibration and consumables; their contract costs are charged separately. Missing instruments produce an explicit unmet-requirement report, not a certification or disclosure of hidden material state. If shaping is attempted, require a separately acquired suitable striker or abrader, stable compatible support, containment and protection appropriate to the actual force and chip hazard. None is supplied by registration. The minimal shaping attempt is one controlled work stroke per round at 1 energy, maximum three strokes per invocation; it is refused before charging if safe placement, supported mechanics or required equipment is missing. Do not turn the weathered source into flint or raise its hardness by shaping. Implement force, fracture, chip trajectory and protection checks before enabling percussion; otherwise retain selection/inspection only. Output is a real candidate, changed workpiece and recoverable fragments or accounted debris, with tool wear; conserve input mass and material identity, and retain pre-existing contamination. Work dissipates effort rather than creating energy. No food is processed by this operation. Commit each completed stroke atomically with event, input/output IDs, costs and accumulated work; pending checks cost nothing. Interruption pauses at stroke boundaries, with partial objects remaining altered. Resume revalidates reach, ownership, equipment and workpiece identity and charges only new work. Cancel or death releases surviving escrow once at its actual location, preserves spent effort, damage and debris, and grants no refund of consumed material or time. There is no unattended shaping or maintenance process. Store tools normally; reinspect after damage or contamination and pay actual cleaning, repair or replacement costs if subsequently needed. Only a carried owned stone/flint candidate whose contact requirements are actually established may be supplied as toolId to thin-slice-food-drying-trial; that trial still performs its own checks and requires moss to learn it separately.\",\"learning\":3,\"experienceReview\":\"Study is three individual simulation rounds at 0.5 energy per round after implementation; registration and study award no experience benefit. Actual newly verified observations, measurements or informative failed tests may provide a small personal information benefit, including learning that a candidate is unsuitable; unknown properties are not information gains. Implement event-qualified deduplication by actor, specimen/property, method and materially changed conditions. At most 0.02 short pleasure per qualifying work/inspection round, capped at 0.04 across ten rounds, decaying to zero within two rounds; at most 0.01 slowly maintained satisfaction from personally applicable completed work, capped at 0.02, decaying 0.002 per inactive round, with no stacking for equivalent functions. Familiar legitimate work may maintain that modest benefit only through new actual work events. Requests, queries, names, registration, learning and mastery give none. No physical comfort, nutrition or safety benefit is inferred. Physical comfort remains globally capped at 10; mood cannot reduce basic nutrition. Implement eligibility, caps and cooldowns in code without changing protected reward accounts, budgets, goals or permissions.\",\"visualReview\":\"Reuse the existing rock/material rendering with general metadata: operation mode, exact workpiece/tool references, material, position, completed stroke count, visible edge outline, actual chips/debris, evidence method, uncertainty and status unverified/failed/measured. Emit selection-observed, stroke-completed, inspection-recorded, blocked and interrupted events only when they occur. An unmeasured edge may look sharp but must not display a passing-tool or food-safe badge. Failed or incomplete strokes never show a completed tool. Risk and instrument requirements are visible as unmet requirements, not as owned objects.\"},{\"actor\":\"ivo\",\"decision\":\"develop\",\"ability\":null,\"reason\":\"The available related search and contracts contain no equivalent operation that mechanically opens an owned shell and separates real contents. probe press is a small material interaction, not an established whole-sample opening and product-separation contract. Reuse its applicable observation/contact code, but develop the missing general operation rather than claiming that a generic probe already yields opened nuts. Ivo already owns a sample; another harvest is unnecessary.\",\"specification\":\"General operation: Mechanically open and inspect shelled material. Parameters: exact inputStackId, one whole unit per attempt, mode open/inspect, optional exact pressureToolIds and supportId, and separation location. It applies to suitable shelled materials for any actor. Initial exact input can be item-14-ivo-138, quantity 2 hazelnut units owned by ivo, origin start-1-nuts; consume at most one unit from this stack per opening attempt. Revalidate current ownership, remaining quantity, reach and condition at execution. Do not assume ownership equals carrying or teleport the stack to the actor. Navigate and pickup are separate at their registered costs. No eating is included. The smallest implementation uses bounded manual compression between suitable acquired pressure surfaces, followed by direct inspection and physical separation. First attempt requires two actual sound, stable pressure surfaces, including a stable lower support on firm ground, adequate light and a place to retain fragments. They may be suitable acquired wooden or stone pieces, but suitability, ownership/authorized access, geometry and load tolerance must be checked; none is granted. Do not disclose moss's remembered stone location to ivo. Ivo can independently inspect accessible material, including known fallen branches such as forest-branch-0 at (17.2,13.3), without assuming a branch is rigid enough. Gathering two accessible loose units, if appropriate, costs two rounds and 4 energy using gather; stock and suitability are checked independently. Travel uses navigate speed 0.8 and distance times 2 energy increased by carried mass; pickup uses its separate contract. No cutter, container, balance or protective equipment is assumed. Open costs one round and 1 energy for one controlled, low-force compression cycle. Fingers must be outside the compression zone, support must be stable and the shell must not present an uncontrolled ejection hazard. No impact, hammering, sharp-shell hand squeezing or repeated force escalation is included in this minimal version. If the mechanics cannot safely open the shell at the supported load, record no opening or partial cracking, retain the real altered sample and report the limitation. Missing pressure/contact mechanics and component separation enter the existing development handoff; share applicable material/contact infrastructure with the tool operation, recording code reuse. Do not fabricate yield to compensate for absent mechanics. Inspection/separation costs one additional round and 0.2 energy and requires the actual sample and fragments in reach. It records visible shell condition, whether opened, apparent contents, visible damage/discoloration and recoverable versus scattered material. Keep recoverable contents and shell in distinct actual ground piles or in separately acquired appropriate receptacles; no free container or food-clean surface. Ground placement is explicitly not a food-safety measure. Split the original unit into kernel/contents, shell and any actual lost fragments using represented composition; if composition is not represented, implement a labeled physical composition model and record its assumptions, not measured nutritional knowledge. Conserve mass, age, existing decay and material constituents; do not create a whole kernel in addition to the intact input. No calibrated balance exists in the supplied facts, so report visible counts, approximate recovery and model accounting separately, not invented measured weights. No inferred toxicity, nutrition, preservation, sterility or safe-consumption status. Completed opening and separation are atomic progress steps with exact input/output references. Interruptions retain the actual intact, cracked or opened state. Resume revalidates item identity, reach and equipment; it does not charge again for completed steps or restore an intact nut. Cancellation returns surviving reserved material once, leaving already separated products at their actual locations; death releases them there. Spent energy, time, tool wear and scattered losses are not refunded. Failed precondition checks do not consume the nut or charge work. Food continues normal aging during real elapsed rounds and after completion; no unattended opening, preservation or decay reset. Check pressure surfaces for new damage before reuse; replacement or cleaning requires actual materials and separate real work, with no automatic maintenance. Actual participants must communicate and act independently; no helper or transferred tool is assumed. Development waiting does not advance the world.\",\"learning\":2,\"experienceReview\":\"Study requires two individual simulation rounds at 0.5 energy per round after implementation; it grants neither mastery to another actor nor experiential rewards. Actual inspection of newly exposed contents or an informative mechanical failure can qualify as personally applicable information gain. Deduplicate by actor, sample/property, method and materially changed conditions; repeating a request or rereading the same result does not qualify. Apply the same shared functional benefit limits as the tool operation: short pleasure at most 0.02 per qualifying event-round and 0.04 per ten rounds, expiring within two rounds; slowly maintained satisfaction at most 0.01 from completed personally applicable work, total cap 0.02 and inactive decay 0.002 per round. Equivalent functions cannot bypass these limits. Familiar real practice may maintain a modest benefit without compulsory novelty. No benefit for naming, registration, queries or mastery; no eating, nutrition, physical comfort or food-safety benefit from opening alone. Preserve protected reward accounts, budgets, goals and permissions; implement all eligibility and decay rules in code. Global physical comfort remains capped at 10 and basic nutrition is independent of mood.\",\"visualReview\":\"Use reusable material-processing metadata: sample and tool IDs, position, operation stage, shell state intact/cracked/open, actual visible contents, distinct shell/content pile IDs, scattered debris, observed defects and evidence quality. Emit compression-attempted, shell-cracked or opened only when supported, separation-completed, inspection-recorded and interrupted/blocked events. A failed compression shows an intact or genuinely partially cracked sample, never a full kernel-success animation. Do not display edible, nutritious, preserved or safe badges from appearance. Instrument-free observations remain explicitly visual and approximate.\"}]}"
}

